.TH Cfr-Debug 1 "2026-10-14" "coffer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cfr-debug \- headless coffer PTY inspector
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cfr-debug
[\fI\,options\/\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fI\,command args...\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cfr-debug
spawns a child process on a pseudo-terminal, pipes its output through
coffer, and renders the resulting grid as plain text.
The coffer output callback is wired back to the PTY, so terminal
queries (DA, DSR, kitty keyboard protocol) receive proper replies.
.PP
Script assertions and
.B wait\-for
search the
.B unified buffer
\(em the scrollback (oldest first) followed by the visible rows \(em so
a TUI whose transcript scrolls off the screen is still assertable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rows\fR, \fB\-r\fR \fIROWS\fR
Terminal rows (default: 24).
.TP
\fB\-\-cols\fR, \fB\-c\fR \fICOLS\fR
Terminal columns (default: 80).
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR, \fB\-w\fR \fISEC\fR
Initial wait in seconds before reading script or rendering (default: 3).
.TP
\fB\-\-script\fR, \fB\-f\fR \fIFILE\fR
Execute commands from a script file. See
.B SCRIPT FILE
below.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR
Save raw PTY output to
.IR FILE .
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-row\fR, \fB\-s\fR \fIROW\fR
Dump a specific row (repeatable). When combined with
.BR \-\-quiet ,
only specified rows are shown.
.TP
\fB\-\-cell\-data\fR, \fB\-d\fR
Dump raw cell data (codepoint, width) alongside rendered text.
.TP
\fB\-\-style\-data\fR, \fB\-S\fR
Dump style information (underline, colors) alongside rendered text.
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR, \fB\-q\fR
Suppress rendering of rows not selected with
.BR \-\-show\-row .
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Set an environment variable for the child (repeatable). Applied after
the built-in
.B TERM
/
.B COLORTERM
/
.BR TERM_PROGRAM ;
an empty
.I VALUE
unsets the variable, including a built-in.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR, \fB\-h\fR
Show help and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\-spec\fR
Emit a machine-readable tab-separated listing for downstream tooling:
.B FLAG
lines for the options, and
.B CMD
lines naming every script command (the feature-detection seam for a
driver that needs a command this build may not have).
.SH SCRIPT FILE
When run with
.BR \-\-script ,
each non-blank, non-comment line is parsed as a command:
.TP
.BI "wait " SECONDS
Drain PTY output for
.I SECONDS
seconds (accepts decimals).
.TP
.BI "wait\-for " "\"TEXT\" [TIMEOUT] [line-end]"
Drain until
.I TEXT
appears in the unified buffer (default timeout: 600 seconds; a timeout
is a failure). The needle is matched as UTF-8. The optional trailing
.B line-end
keyword anchors the match to a row that ends with
.IR TEXT .
.TP
.BI "send " TEXT
Send
.I TEXT
to the PTY. Backslash escapes are expanded:
.B \en
= LF,
.B \er
= CR,
.B \ee
= ESC,
.B \et
= TAB,
.B \exNN
= byte NN (hex),
.B \e\e
= backslash.
.TP
.BI "sendln " TEXT
Like
.BR send ,
with a trailing CR LF.
.TP
.BI "emit " TEXT
Feed
.I TEXT
straight into coffer's terminal parser, bypassing the child (same
escape expansion as
.BR send ).
.TP
.BI "emit\-raw " "HEX [HEX ...]"
Feed literal bytes straight into coffer's parser.
.TP
.BI "raw " "HEX [HEX ...]"
Send literal bytes specified as space-separated hex pairs
(e.g.\&
.BR "raw ff fc 01" ).
.TP
.BI "assert\-contains " TEXT
Fail with exit code 1 if the unified buffer does not contain
.IR TEXT .
.TP
.BI "assert\-not\-contains " TEXT
Fail with exit code 1 if the unified buffer contains
.IR TEXT .
.TP
.BI "await\-exit " "[TIMEOUT]"
Drain until the child exits (default timeout: 10 seconds; a timeout is
a failure) and record its exit status.
.TP
.BI "assert\-exit " STATUS
Fail with exit code 1 unless
.B await\-exit
recorded
.IR STATUS .
.TP
.BI "resize " "COLS ROWS"
Resize the PTY and the grid. On POSIX the child's terminal is resized
with
.BR TIOCSWINSZ ,
so it receives
.BR SIGWINCH ;
on Windows
.B ResizePseudoConsole
is used.
.TP
.BI "render " "[visible|scrollback|all]"
Dump the grid (default:
.BR visible ).
.B scrollback
prints the scrollback, oldest first, with unified row numbers (negative
= scrollback depth);
.B all
prints both.
.TP
.BI "render cells " "ROW [C0 C1]"
Dump per-cell detail (codepoint, width, style, hyperlink id) for
.IR ROW ,
columns
.I C0
through
.I C1
(default: the whole row). Rows are unified coordinates: negative values
address the scrollback
.RB ( \-1
= most recently scrolled off).
.TP
.BI "render styles " ROW
Dump style detail (underline, colors, attributes) for
.IR ROW .
.TP
.B cursor
Dump the cursor state (row, col, visible, blink).
.TP
.B dump\-sixel
Dump live images and placements (id, anchor row/col, pixel size).
.TP
.B quit
End the script run early (success).
.TP
.BI "# " comment
Lines starting with
.B #
are ignored.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Capture the initial screen of crush:
.EX
cfr-debug \-c 68 \-r 20 \-w 5 \-\- crush
.EE
.TP
Scripted CI test with assertions:
.EX
cfr-debug \-r 24 \-c 80 \-f test.script \-\- sh \-c "echo hello world"
.EE
where
.I test.script
might be:
.EX
wait\-for "hello world" 5
assert\-contains "hello world"
await\-exit 5
assert\-exit 0
.EE
.TP
Pin a color tier by unsetting the built-in
.BR COLORTERM :
.EX
cfr-debug \-\-env COLORTERM= \-\- my-tui
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; all assertions passed (if any).
.TP
.B 1
An assertion failed, or a runtime error occurred.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM
The child process sees
.BR xterm\-256color .
.TP
.B COLORTERM
The child process sees
.BR truecolor .
.TP
.B TERM_PROGRAM
The child process sees
.BR ghostty .
.PP
All three can be overridden with
.BR \-\-env .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR coffer (7)
.SH BUGS
No interactive input \(em all input is scripted via
.BR \-\-script .
No mouse support.
.PP
.B assert\-contains
and
.B assert\-not\-contains
search the whole unified buffer (scrollback included), not just the
visible screen; that is a change from the visible-only search of
earlier releases.
